From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lokbondo Kung <lokokung@google.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:24:25 -0800
Subject: [native] Fix shared memory EndAccess after device loss/destruction.

- Prior to this change, when the device is lost or destroyed while a
  SharedTextureMemory or SharedBufferMemory access is open, the work
  recorded during that access may never run, and EndAccess could
  misreport the resource as initialized or use freed Vulkan objects.
- This change validates that the device is alive before calling into
  the backend in EndAccess. If the device is lost, the backend part of
  EndAccess is skipped entirely and an error is returned, so EndAccess
  returns wgpu::Status::Error and no new fence is exported.
- When the backend part of EndAccess fails, including because the
  device is lost, a resource that was used during the access is now
  reported as uninitialized. A resource that wasn't used during the
  access keeps the initialized state that was set on BeginAccess.
- This change also adds regression tests.

Bug: 577360270, 577377985, 495450692
Change-Id: If09e7d267a395755050cea51e5708474e41cd7d4
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/354295
Commit-Queue: Loko Kung <lokokung@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
This branch's Dawn has no MaybeUnknownError/ResultOrUnknownError and SharedResourceMemory::Resource exposes IsInitialized() rather than IsResourceInitialized(); the EndAccess changes use the branch's MaybeError/ResultOrError types and IsInitialized(). The new white-box tests in src/dawn/tests/white_box/SharedTextureMemoryTests.{h,cpp} were not carried: they depend on the newer wgpu::Status-returning BeginAccess API and a CheckCleared helper that do not exist on this branch.

diff --git a/src/dawn/native/SharedResourceMemory.cpp b/src/dawn/native/SharedResourceMemory.cpp
index e124fdf4dfd1a1182c29a5d4fc9769377acbd1fa..3d8bc744db580e46fd79ef2e2d60caf02c23e140 100644
--- a/src/dawn/native/SharedResourceMemory.cpp
+++ b/src/dawn/native/SharedResourceMemory.cpp
@@ -313,13 +313,15 @@ MaybeError SharedResourceMemory::EndAccess(Resource* resource, EndAccessState* s
 
     DAWN_CHECK(!resource->IsError());
     ExecutionSerial lastUsageSerial = resource->OnEndAccess();
+    // If the last usage serial is non-zero, the resource was used by GPU commands during this
+    // access.
+    const bool usedDuringAccess = lastUsageSerial != kBeginningOfGPUTime;
 
-    // If the last usage serial is non-zero, the texture was used.
-    // Call the error-generating part of the EndAccess implementation to export a fence.
-    // This is separated out because writing the output state must happen regardless of whether
-    // or not EndAccessInternal succeeds.
+    // If the resource was used, call the error-generating part of the EndAccess implementation to
+    // export a fence. This is separated out because writing the output state must happen
+    // regardless of whether or not EndAccessInternal succeeds.
     MaybeError err;
-    if (lastUsageSerial != kBeginningOfGPUTime) {
+    if (usedDuringAccess) {
         ResultOrError<FenceAndSignalValue> result =
             EndAccessInternal(lastUsageSerial, resource, state);
         if (result.IsSuccess()) {
@@ -350,7 +352,16 @@ MaybeError SharedResourceMemory::EndAccess(Resource* resource, EndAccessState* s
         state->fences = {};
         state->signaledValues = {};
     }
-    state->initialized = resource->IsInitialized();
+    // If EndAccessInternal failed, including because the device is lost (or destroyed), commands
+    // using the resource during this access may not have been flushed, may have been dropped
+    // without ever executing (e.g. a queue.writeTexture recorded in a passive pending command
+    // context, or a submit that failed), or may have been in the middle of executing when the
+    // device was lost, even though the resource was already marked as initialized on the CPU side.
+    // In that case, conservatively report the resource as uninitialized so that the next user
+    // lazily clears it instead of reading back undefined contents. If the resource wasn't used
+    // during the access, its initialized state is still the one set on BeginAccess.
+    bool dirtyDueToErrors = !err.IsSuccess() && usedDuringAccess;
+    state->initialized = resource->IsInitialized() && !dirtyDueToErrors;
     return err;
 }
 
@@ -359,12 +370,15 @@ ResultOrError<FenceAndSignalValue> SharedResourceMemory::EndAccessInternal(
     ExecutionSerial lastUsageSerial,
     Resource* resource,
     EndAccessState* rawState) {
+    // If the device is lost (including when it is destroyed), the backend can't record or submit
+    // any more commands, and the commands using the resource may have been dropped, so there is
+    // nothing to export for them. Return an error so that EndAccess reports the resource as
+    // uninitialized, and so that the backend part of EndAccess is skipped entirely.
+    DAWN_TRY(GetDevice()->ValidateIsAlive());
     UnpackedPtr<EndAccessState> state;
     DAWN_TRY_ASSIGN(state, ValidateAndUnpack(rawState));
-    if (!GetDevice()->IsLost()) {
-        // Ensure that commands are submitted before exporting fences with the last usage serial.
-        DAWN_TRY(GetDevice()->GetQueue()->EnsureCommandsFlushed(lastUsageSerial));
-    }
+    // Ensure that commands are submitted before exporting fences with the last usage serial.
+    DAWN_TRY(GetDevice()->GetQueue()->EnsureCommandsFlushed(lastUsageSerial));
     return EndAccessImpl(resource, lastUsageSerial, state);
 }
 
